    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386">

                <pb facs="0524" n="266" xml:id="pg266"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/3710</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 14, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s 11th. After cabling 12th, authorities decided to consult Cabinet
                    respecting exports from Belgium and will not decide particular questions until
                    Cabinet acts. Will continue to press Welsch and Culley case.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
